#EXTM3U
# QA fixture for D-ID-1 (docs/STATUS.md): the provider list BEFORE a password
# rotation. list-v2.m3u is byte-identical except that the path segment after
# /live/ differs on every stream URL; that segment stands in for the
# credential slot of an Xtream URL and is NOT a credential. Read README.md.
#
# A. six rows with no tvg-id and a unique name: legacy u:<fnv1a32(url)>,
#    scheme 2 n:<fnv1a32(folded name)>. These MUST move.
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="News",Alpha News
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/alpha.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sports",Bravo Sports
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/bravo.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Kids",Charlie Kids
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/charlie.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Movies",Delta Movies
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/delta.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Music",Echo Music
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/echo.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Docs",Foxtrot Docs
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/foxtrot.m3u8
# B. one tvg-id shared by an HD/SD pair with distinct names: the tvg-id is
#    not unique so legacy falls to u:, the names are unique so scheme 2 is
#    n:. These MUST move, through the non-unique-id path.
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="golf.test" tvg-name="Golf" group-title="Sports",Golf HD
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/golf-hd.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="golf.test" tvg-name="Golf" group-title="Sports",Golf SD
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/golf-sd.m3u8
# C. four rows with a unique tvg-id: t:<tvg-id> under both schemes. These
#    must NOT move, and their ids survive the rotation on their own.
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="hotel.test" group-title="News",Hotel TV
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/hotel.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="india.test" group-title="News",India TV
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/india.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="juliet.test" group-title="News",Juliet TV
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/juliet.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 tvg-id="kilo.test" group-title="News",Kilo TV
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/kilo.m3u8
# D. exactly one colliding-name pair: no tvg-id, byte-identical names,
#    different URLs. The name key is refused, both stay u:, and both are
#    orphaned by the rotation. This is D-ID-2's accepted limit, observable.
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sports",Lima Twins
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/lima-a.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sports",Lima Twins
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/lima-b.m3u8
# E. two DIFFERENT names whose folded fnv1a32 collide (both n:e63189cb).
#    The uniqueness test runs on the hashed key, so both are refused and
#    stay u:, exactly like D. Found by brute force through name_id_key.
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sports",Hash Twin 132789
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/hash-a.m3u8
#EXTINF:-1 group-title="Sports",Hash Twin 729192
http://rotate.example.test/live/k1/hash-b.m3u8
